{"authored" [{"question" "q-72005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $g(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂g}{∂x}=\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nFind the set of real values $(x,y)$ where all partial derivatives of $g$ exist. Choose the displayed set that expresses the required condition on $x^2+y^2$ explicitly as a strict positivity inequality." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-72005/review.json" "file_sha256" "df8288b3197390c941d262a5deeff1bb36f40cb81ebc69e413b40e6343d20682" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-72005/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "8c4e88374ad7d95886eaf237603830fa83c7ebb080e42fb360c24f75f9187028" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-72005/verification.json" "basis" 1629 "rationale" "The original radio prompt asks only for a domain and supplies two mathematically equivalent valid sets c and e; the source accepted e. The authorized study correction explicitly requests a strict positivity inequality, preserving all original g/derivative mathematics, choices and the accepted key while explaining c’s equivalence. It versions field ownership and retains original capture evidence, answer entities and database history."} {"question" "q-72005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For real $x$ and $y$, each square is nonnegative, so $x^2+y^2\\ge 0$. Their sum equals zero exactly when $x=y=0$. Consequently,\n\n$$\nx^2+y^2\\ne 0\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad x^2+y^2>0.\n$$\n\nThe logarithm in $g(x,y)=x\\ln(x^2+y^2)$ requires $x^2+y^2>0$. This same condition makes the denominators in both supplied partial derivatives nonzero. On this open set the logarithm and rational terms are differentiable, so both partial derivatives exist. At the origin the original function is undefined, so its partial derivatives do not exist there.\n\nThus the domain where all partial derivatives exist is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x^2+y^2>0\\}=\\mathbb R^2\\setminus\\{(0,0)\\}.\n$$\n\nThe choices using $x^2+y^2\\ne 0$ (c) and $x^2+y^2>0$ (e) describe exactly the same domain. The question explicitly requests the strict positivity form, so choose e. Choice c is an equivalent description of the domain, but it does not express the condition as the requested positivity inequality." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-72005/review.json" "file_sha256" "df8288b3197390c941d262a5deeff1bb36f40cb81ebc69e413b40e6343d20682" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-72005/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "8c4e88374ad7d95886eaf237603830fa83c7ebb080e42fb360c24f75f9187028" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-72005/verification.json" "basis" 1629 "rationale" "The original radio prompt asks only for a domain and supplies two mathematically equivalent valid sets c and e; the source accepted e. The authorized study correction explicitly requests a strict positivity inequality, preserving all original g/derivative mathematics, choices and the accepted key while explaining c’s equivalence. It versions field ownership and retains original capture evidence, answer entities and database history."} {"question" "q-72005" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0}"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-72005/review.json" "file_sha256" "df8288b3197390c941d262a5deeff1bb36f40cb81ebc69e413b40e6343d20682" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-72005/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "8c4e88374ad7d95886eaf237603830fa83c7ebb080e42fb360c24f75f9187028" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-72005/verification.json" "basis" 1629 "rationale" "The original radio prompt asks only for a domain and supplies two mathematically equivalent valid sets c and e; the source accepted e. The authorized study correction explicitly requests a strict positivity inequality, preserving all original g/derivative mathematics, choices and the accepted key while explaining c’s equivalence. It versions field ownership and retains original capture evidence, answer entities and database history."} {"question" "q-72005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $g(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂g}{∂x}=\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nfind the set of values $(x,y)$ where all partial derivatives of $g$ exist." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043502/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a842aaa5c66bd6200841247aa79041d02cdfac938205cf33f18021cf667699c" "basis" 1625 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043502/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-72005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that $g(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ is defined only when ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0.$ So, the domain of $g$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{g}={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function ${g}_{x}(x,y)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ is defined only when ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0.$ So, the domain of ${g}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{g}_{x}}={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0}.\n$$\n\n- The function ${g}_{y}(x,y)=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ is defined only when ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${g}_{y}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{g}_{y}}={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partials of $g$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{g}\\cap {D}_{{g}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{g}_{y}} & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0}\\cap {(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0}\\cap {(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0} \\\\  & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043502/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a842aaa5c66bd6200841247aa79041d02cdfac938205cf33f18021cf667699c" "basis" 1625 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043502/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-72005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043502/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8160a39dc8de687c2bddf726a8d167f584cd484dc388c7c85c8e49cacf0fbd57" "basis" 1625 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043502/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [] "usage" {"q-72005" []} "basis" 1629 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186321099 17592186321100 17592186321101 17592186321102 17592186321103] "immutable_fields" [[17592186321372 :answer-field/correct] [17592186321372 :answer-field/id] [17592186321372 :answer-field/key] [17592186321372 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
